infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Tuning the cooldown: too short vs too long
  desc Cooldown = how long the breaker stays open before probing. The right value tracks the dependency's real recovery time.
  compares
    - label Too short (Hystrix ~5 s default)
      children
        - label Probes before recovery
          desc The trial hits a still-broken service, fails, and the breaker reopens
        - label Flapping between states
          desc open to half-open fires too fast and oscillates, sending bursts of doomed calls
        - label Wasted trial budget
          desc Repeated failed probes keep load on a dependency that has not healed
    - label Too long (resilience4j ~60 s default)
      children
        - label Rejects a recovered service
          desc The dependency healed seconds ago but every caller still gets fast-failed
        - label Self-inflicted outage
          desc A short downstream blip is stretched into a long outage you caused
        - label Match it to recovery time
          desc A service that restarts in ~10 s wants ~10 s, not 60 s and not 1 s
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b
